codex
The sealed benchmark reports 20 `NAME_ONLY` positives; I’m extracting those programmatically so the proposal file has exactly the benchmark rows rather than hand-copied guesses.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "python -c \"import json; p=json.load(open('registry/search_benchmark.json', encoding='utf-8')); rows=[]
for slug,t in p['topics'].items():
    for x in t['positives']:
        if x.get('identifier_state')=='NAME_ONLY' or (not x.get('pmid') and not x.get('nct') and not x.get('doi')):
            rows.append((slug,x.get('trial'),x.get('note'),x.get('source_path')))
print(len(rows))
for i,r in enumerate(rows,1): print(i, repr(r[0]), repr(r[1]), repr(r[2]), repr(r[3]))\"" in C:\mh-r-R3
 succeeded in 258ms:
20
1 'colchicine-postop-af' 'five audit-named trials' 'mechanism=concept-query; status=audit_identified; k=3->8 per audit; names pending external verification | NAME_ONLY: can only be scored by normalized title match' 'docs/known_eligible_missing.json'
2 'colchicine-recurrent-pericarditis' 'ICAP' 'mechanism=access-tier; status=verification_failed; VERIFIED AGAINST SOURCE (PMID 23992557): population is ACUTE (first-episode) pericarditis, NOT the recurrent-pericarditis population of this topic; and the audit-cited counts 11/120 vs 25/120 (9.2%/20.8%) do NOT match the abstract (primary incessant-or-recurrent ~37.5% placebo, symptom persistence 19.2%). Eligibility CONTESTED (population axis) and counts unverified -- NOT integrated; recovery refused. | NAME_ONLY: can only be scored by normalized title match' 'docs/known_eligible_missing.json'
