docs\search_recall_regression_corpus_search_v2.json:3: "validation_status": "REGRESSION_CORPUS — not prospective validation: all 32 corpus topics are disqualified as held-out (exposed through audits, URLs, commit history); measured on the 5 corpus topics that had zero contact with engine tuning",
docs\search_recall_regression_corpus.json:3: "validation_status": "REGRESSION_CORPUS — not prospective validation: all 32 corpus topics are disqualified as held-out (exposed through audits, URLs, commit history); measured on the 5 corpus topics that had zero contact with engine tuning",
docs\search_recall.json:7: "improvement_provenance": "recall rose because the QUERY improved (concept + class expansion + pagination), NOT because the test set grew or a verification state was loosened; the denominator is the same 6 SOURCE_VERIFIED_ELIGIBLE trials. The one apparent miss during measurement (TECOS) was a wrong target PMID in the harness (26105174, a cardiomyopathy case report) corrected to the real TECOS PMID 26052984 -- a harness error, not a search failure or a test-set change.",
docs\search_recall.json:12:  {"trial": "TECOS", "topic": "dpp4-mace-t2d", "pmid": "26052984", "hits_in_boolean_set": 1833, "recalled": true, "via": "sitagliptin AND type 2 diabetes AND RCT"},
docs\search_provenance.json:2: "_doc": "P0 (round-2 doac-vte + sglt2-ckd): 'registry-first systematic search' is contradicted by our own audit trail on multiple topics — the AACT registry run FAILED (RAN_ERROR) and/or PubMed was queried with UID/PMID-anchored strings for already-known trials. A fetch of a named identifier is not a search (standing memory law). This classifies how each topic's included set was actually assembled. PRELIMINARY: the 5 PMID_ENUMERATION are from explicit protocol 'UID-anchored' wording; the 21 UNCLEAR need the verbatim PubMed query strings checked, but the TWO independently audited among them (doac-vte, sglt2-ckd) BOTH proved PMID-enumeration, so the true PMID_ENUMERATION count is likely far higher.",
docs\search_provenance.json:5:    "note": "Registry-first (AACT) = RAN_ERROR; the source_status table shows it, but the search narrative still presents the topic as registry-first. RAN_ERROR must never be rendered as a completed search (extends the audit-22 NOT_RUN gate limb to RAN_ERROR)."},
docs\search_provenance.json:8:  "needs_verbatim_query_check": {"n": 21, "note": "protocol prose did not state the query type; the verbatim PubMed queries must be inspected. doac-vte and sglt2-ckd (independently audited) both turned out PMID-enumeration, so expect most of these to be enumeration too."}
docs\search_provenance.json:10: "headline": "At least 11 of 32 topics do NOT have a genuine executed concept search (6 registry-first RAN_ERROR-rendered + 5 explicit PMID-enumeration); the 21 unclear likely include many more (2 of 2 audited among them were enumeration). Every PMID-enumeration topic must say so on the page and must not claim a registry-first/systematic search.",
protocols\dpp4-mace-t2d.md:44:- PubMed: direct UID queries for SAVOR-TIMI 53, EXAMINE, TECOS, CARMELINA, and
protocols\dpp4-mace-t2d.md:61:- **TECOS** - NCT00790205; positive-control PMID 26052984.
protocols\dpp4-mace-t2d.md:64:- **Positive** - the search must recover and include TECOS (PMID 26052984).
topics\empagliflozin-hfpef-hosp.json:131:  "comparator_scope_note": "k=1 CONTRIBUTING, not a complete-evidence claim: EMPEROR-Preserved (NCT03057951) supplies the only EXTRACTABLE primary-outcome estimate here. This is NOT a claim that the eligible evidence base is a single trial -- 4 records screened in and 3 are declared absent for this pooled number. External audit identified EMPA-VISION (a randomised double-blind trial with a separate HFpEF cohort) as eligible and missed by the trial-level search; the cohort-level screening + concept-query rebuild is the fix. The nearest published synthesis pools the SGLT2-inhibitor CLASS (a broader, network-level PICO), so its larger k is a scope difference, not evidence this review failed to retrieve."
topics\dapagliflozin-hfpef-hosp.json:156:  "comparator_scope_note": "k=1 CONTRIBUTING, not a complete-evidence claim: DELIVER (NCT03619213) supplies the only EXTRACTABLE primary-outcome estimate here. This is NOT a claim that the eligible evidence base is a single trial -- 5 records screened in for this PICO and 4 are declared absent for this pooled number (no extractable primary estimate in the committed source). External audit also flagged further eligible HFpEF records (e.g. an EMPA-VISION-style cohort design) that a trial-level search can miss; the concept-query search rebuild is the fix. The nearest published synthesis pools the SGLT2-inhibitor CLASS (a broader, network-level PICO), so its larger k is a scope difference, not evidence this review failed to retrieve."
docs\definition_audit.json:2: "_doc": "Cross-family definition audit (Gemini 3.1 Pro via AGY + Fable, EVERY pooled row): does the extracted result match the outcome LABEL definition (composite component set, timepoint, population, analysis set), not just the number. The TECOS class. Candidates hand-adjudicated; a model call is a source (raw outputs scratchpad/defaudit).",
