docs\definition_audit.json:208:   "resolution": "DISCLOSED (composite-component difference, found by the cross-family AGY/Gemini audit of the not-yet-audited topics): DAPA-HF (31535829) defines its primary as worsening heart failure — HF HOSPITALISATION or an URGENT HF VISIT requiring IV therapy — or cardiovascular death, whereas EMPEROR-Reduced (32865377) and our outcome label count CV death or HF hospitalisation only. The urgent-visit component is a minor broadening in DAPA-HF; disclosed, still poolable.",
