=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>TRACES tranexamic acid postpartum haemorrhage placebo</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>LEGACY_UNRECORDED</td><td><code>tranexamic acid AND (post-partum haemorrhage OR postpartum haemorrhage OR postpartum hemorrhage) AND (WOMAN OR death due to bleeding) AND (randomised OR randomized OR trial) || oral tranexamic acid adjunct postpartum hemorrhage placebo randomized || TRACES tranexamic acid postpartum haemorrhage placebo</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_OK</strong>: ran and returned records</td><td>unknown -&gt; 54 -&gt; 54</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>no</td></tr></table><h4>Source status (which adapters ran)</h4><p class='muted'>Citation chase: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · ClinicalTrials.gov: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Europe PMC (OA + metadata): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Legacy unrecorded retrieval: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · PMC full text: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · PubMed: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Registry-first (AACT): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> — RAN_OK = ran and returned records; RAN_ZERO = ran, none matched; RAN_ERROR = attempted but failed; NOT_RUN = not attempted for this topic.</p><h4>Retrieval class</h4><div class='absent'><p><strong>TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL — DISCOVERY-BIASED, NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH</strong> We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic. an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process.</p></div><table class='recs'><tr><th>Verbatim query</th><th>Kind</th><th>Features fired</th></tr><tr><td><code>tranexamic acid AND (post-partum haemorrhage OR postpartum haemorrhage OR postpartum hemorrhage) AND (WOMAN OR death due to bleeding) AND (randomised OR randomized OR trial)</code></td><td>NAME_SEEDED</td><td>trial_acronym_token:WOMAN</td></tr><tr><td><code>oral tranexamic acid adjunct postpartum hemorrhage placebo randomized</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>TRACES tranexamic acid postpartum haemorrhage placebo</code></td><td>NAME_SEEDED</td><td>trial_acronym_token:TRACES</td></tr><tr><td><code>tranexamic acid AND (post-partum haemorrhage OR postpartum haemorrhage OR postpartum hemorrhage) AND (WOMAN OR death due to bleeding) AND (randomised OR randomized OR trial) || oral tranexamic acid adjunct postpartum hemorrhage placebo randomized || TRACES tranexamic acid postpartum haemorrhage placebo</code></td><td>NAME_SEEDED</td><td>trial_acronym_token:WOMAN; trial_acronym_token:TRACES</td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>RAN_OK</strong>; its evidence set was assembled by TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL (title/name-anchored queries for pre-identified trials), which cannot discover an unknown eligible trial. A query seeded with the names of known trials is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>Positive-control recovery (NOT systematic-review recall)</h4><p>Positive-control recovery: the committed registry query re-found <strong>2/3</strong> of this topic's PRE-SPECIFIED known trials (pooled + declared positive controls; enumerated 33; status RAN_OK). Reachable ceiling <strong>3/3</strong>: 1 trial(s) are registered but not enumerated by the committed query (registry vocabulary limit — improvable). <span class='muted'>Missed: 36243576.</span> <span class='muted'>Measured 2026-09-11T23:39:14Z.</span> <strong>This is not systematic-review recall.</strong> It measures whether the committed registry query re-finds the trials ALREADY KNOWN to the build; a trial that was never in the known set is not in the denominator, so a high value does <strong>not</strong> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>33</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 12 have a linked publication; <strong>2</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 11 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>tranexamic acid AND (post-partum haemorrhage OR postpartum haemorrhage OR postpartum hemorrhage) AND (WOMAN OR death due to bleeding) AND (randomised OR randomized OR trial)</pre><pre class='query'>oral tranexamic acid adjunct postpartum hemorrhage placebo randomized</pre><pre class='query'>TRACES tranexamic acid postpartum haemorrhage placebo</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;postpartum hemorrhage&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;tranexamic acid&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier names tranexamic acid; all included records map to that agent. Verdict: <code>MATCH</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n</th></tr><tr><td>Records identified (committed search)</td><td>76</td></tr><tr><td>Records screened (deduplicated)</td><td>76</td></tr><tr><td>Excluded at screening — by rule</td><td>72 (X1 30 · X2 38 · X3 4)</td></tr><tr><td>Met eligibility (P/I/C/design)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pooled in the primary outcome (k)</strong></td><td><strong>1</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Eligible but outcome not extracted from the abstract (full-text pass pending)</td><td>3</td></tr></table><p class='note'>Every excluded record's rule id, reason and verbatim span are listed below (PRISMA item 16b: exclusions with reasons).</p><h4>Dual independent screening (PRISMA item 8)</h4><p>Two independently-implemented rule screeners over 76 records: agreement <strong>76/76</strong>, disagreement <strong>0.0%</strong> (0 records). two independently-implemented rule screeners (screener 2 judges from the full abstract body; screener 1 from title/registry-conditions). Adjudicator: screener 1. <em>the two rule sets share an author and the same eligibility criteria, so they are NOT statistically independent; this agreement overstates inter-rater reliability. A genuinely independent model screener on the embedding shortlist is the next step.</em></p><p class='note'><strong>Trial integrity:</strong> none of the 1 trials pooled across all outcomes on this page is retracted (checked 2026-09-13T08:44:31Z via PubMed efetch (PublicationType + CommentsCorrections) + AACT dates).</p><p>76 records screened; <strong>4 included</strong>. Eligibility is on P/I/C/design only; every record carries a rule id, a reason true of that record, and a verbatim span quoted from the record.</p><table class='recs'><tr><th>Record</th><th>Type</th><th>Decision</th><th>Rule</th><th>Found by</th><th>Reason (true of the record)</th><th>Ver