_tag:[Title]; title_field_tag:[Title]</td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>RAN_OK</strong>; its evidence set was assembled by TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL (title/name-anchored queries for pre-identified trials), which cannot discover an unknown eligible trial. A query seeded with the names of known trials is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>Positive-control recovery (NOT systematic-review recall)</h4><p>Positive-control recovery: the committed registry query re-found <strong>2/3</strong> of this topic's PRE-SPECIFIED known trials (pooled + declared positive controls; enumerated 53; status RAN_OK). Reachable ceiling <strong>3/3</strong>: 1 trial(s) are registered but not enumerated by the committed query (registry vocabulary limit — improvable). <span class='muted'>Missed: 33933206.</span> <span class='muted'>Measured 2026-09-11T23:39:14Z.</span> <strong>This is not systematic-review recall.</strong> It measures whether the committed registry query re-finds the trials ALREADY KNOWN to the build; a trial that was never in the known set is not in the denominator, so a high value does <strong>not</strong> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>53</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 14 have a linked publication; <strong>4</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 20 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>((Tocilizumab[Title] AND patients[Title] AND admitted[Title] AND hospital[Title] AND COVID-19[Title]) OR (Tocilizumab[Title] AND Patients[Title] AND Hospitalized[Title] AND Covid-19[Title] AND Pneumonia[Title]) OR (Tocilizumab[Title] AND Hospitalized[Title] AND Severe[Title] AND Covid-19[Title] AND Pneumonia[Title])) NOT (post-hoc[Title] OR posthoc[Title] OR biomarker[Title] OR biomarkers[Title] OR antibody[Title] OR antibodies[Title] OR systematic[Title] OR meta-analysis[Title] OR review[Title] OR retrospective[Title] OR cohort[Title] OR reply[Title] OR case-control[Title] OR challenge[Title] OR real-life[Title] OR comparison[Title] OR baricitinib[Title] OR colchicine[Title])</pre><pre class='query'>((Efficacy[Title] AND Tocilizumab[Title] AND Patients[Title] AND Hospitalized[Title] AND Covid-19[Title]) OR (Effect[Title] AND Tocilizumab[Title] AND Usual[Title] AND Care[Title] AND Adults[Title] AND Hospitalized[Title] AND COVID-19[Title]) OR (Effect[Title] AND Tocilizumab[Title] AND Standard[Title] AND Care[Title] AND Clinical[Title] AND Worsening[Title])) NOT (post-hoc[Title] OR posthoc[Title] OR biomarker[Title] OR biomarkers[Title] OR antibody[Title] OR antibodies[Title] OR systematic[Title] OR meta-analysis[Title] OR review[Title] OR retrospective[Title] OR cohort[Title] OR reply[Title] OR case-control[Title] OR challenge[Title] OR real-life[Title] OR comparison[Title] OR baricitinib[Title] OR colchicine[Title])</pre><pre clas