itle]</td></tr><tr><td><code>Hydrocortisone[Title] COVID-19[Title] randomized clinical trial mortality</code></td><td>TITLE_ANCHORED</td><td>title_field_tag:[Title]; title_field_tag:[Title]</td></tr><tr><td><code>Metcovid methylprednisolone hospitalized COVID-19 randomized placebo mortality</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>Dexamethasone[Title] Covid-19[Title] randomized controlled trial mortality usual care || Hydrocortisone[Title] COVID-19[Title] randomized clinical trial mortality || Metcovid methylprednisolone hospitalized COVID-19 randomized placebo mortality</code></td><td>TITLE_ANCHORED</td><td>title_field_tag:[Title]; title_field_tag:[Title]; title_field_tag:[Title]; title_field_tag:[Title]</td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>RAN_OK</strong>; its evidence set was assembled by TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL (title/name-anchored queries for pre-identified trials), which cannot discover an unknown eligible trial. A query seeded with the names of known trials is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>Positive-control recovery (NOT systematic-review recall)</h4><p>Positive-control recovery: the committed registry query re-found <strong>2/3</strong> of this topic's PRE-SPECIFIED known trials (pooled + declared positive controls; enumerated 95; status RAN_OK). Reachable ceiling <strong>3/3</strong>: 1 trial(s) are registered but not enumerated by the committed query (registry vocabulary limit — improvable). <span class='muted'>Missed: 32785710.</span> <span class='muted'>Measured 2026-09-11T23:39:14Z.</span> <strong>This is not systematic-review recall.</strong> It measures whether the committed registry query re-finds the trials ALREADY KNOWN to the build; a trial that was never in the known set is not in the denominator, so a high value does <strong>not</strong> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>95</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 39 have a linked publication; <strong>3</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 27 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>Dexamethasone[Title] Covid-19[Title] randomized controlled trial mortality usual care</pre><pre class='query'>Hydrocortisone[Title] COVID-19[Title] randomized clinical trial mortality</pre><pre class='query'>Metcovid methylprednisolone hospitalized COVID-19 randomized placebo mortality</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;COVID-19&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;dexamethasone&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier leading token matches class term corticosteroids. Verdict: <code>NOT_APPLICABLE</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n