NOT_RUN = not attempted for this topic.</p><h4>Retrieval class</h4><div class='absent'><p><strong>HAND-WRITTEN KEYWORD SEARCH — NOT A REGISTERED CONCEPT SEARCH; NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH</strong> We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic. an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process.</p></div><table class='recs'><tr><th>Verbatim query</th><th>Kind</th><th>Features fired</th></tr><tr><td><code>hydrocortisone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>methylprednisolone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality NOT macrolides NOT post-hoc NOT lymphopenia NOT biomarkers</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>(prednisone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized clinical stability NOT diabetic NOT pathogen NOT biomarker NOT antibiotic-specific NOT cosyntropin NOT allocation NOT estimation) OR (dexamethasone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized hospital stay NOT biomarkers NOT troponin NOT neutrophil NOT lymphocyte NOT pleural NOT pediatric NOT children)</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>hydrocortisone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality || methylprednisolone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality NOT macrolides NOT post-hoc NOT lymphopenia NOT biomarkers || (prednisone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized clinical stability NOT diabetic NOT pathogen NOT biomarker NOT antibiotic-specific NOT cosyntropin NOT allocation NOT estimation) OR (dexamethasone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized hospital stay NOT biomarkers NOT troponin NOT neutrophil NOT lymphocyte NOT pleural NOT pediatric NOT children)</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>NOT_RUN</strong>; its PubMed queries are hand-written keyword strings that were never registered as a concept search, whose discovery reach is unmeasured — a zero here reads as not observed, never as absent. A hand-written keyword query is not a documented systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>hydrocortisone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality</pre><pre class='query'>methylprednisolone severe community-acquired pneumonia randomized placebo mortality NOT macrolides NOT post-hoc NOT lymphopenia NOT biomarkers</pre><pre class='query'>(prednisone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized clinical stability NOT diabetic NOT pathogen NOT biomarker NOT antibiotic-specific NOT cosyntropin NOT allocation NOT estimation) OR (dexamethasone community-acquired pneumonia placebo randomized hospital stay NOT biomarkers NOT troponin NOT neutrophil NOT lymphocyte NOT pleural NOT pediatric NOT children)</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;community-acquired pneumonia&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;hydrocortisone&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier leading token matches class term corticosteroids. Verdict: <code>NOT_APPLICABLE</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n</th></tr><tr><td>Records identified (committed search)</td><td>114</td></tr><tr><td>Records screened (deduplicated)</td><td>114</td></tr><tr><td>Excluded at screening — by rule</td><td>105 (X1 92 · X2 10 · X3 3)</td></tr><tr><td>Met eligibility (P/I/C/design)</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pooled in the primary outcome (k)</strong></td><td><strong>2</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Eligible but outcome not extracted from the abstract (full-text pass pending)</td><td>7</td></tr></table><p class='note'>Every excluded record's rule id, reason and verbatim span are listed below (PRISMA item 16b: exclusions with reasons).</p><h4>Dual independent screening (PRISMA item 8)</h4><p>Two independently-implemented rule screeners over 114 records: agreement <strong>114/114</strong>, disagreement <strong>0.0%</strong> (0 records). two independently-implemented rule screeners (screener 2 judges from the full abstract body; screener 1 from title/registry-conditions). Adjudicator: screener 1. <em>the two rule sets share an author and the same eligibility criteria, so they are NOT statistically independent; this agreement overstates inter-rater reliability. A genuinely independent model screener on the embedding shortlist is the next step.</em></p><p class='note'><strong>Trial integrity:</strong> none of the 3 trials pooled across all outcomes on this page is retracted; 1 registered retrospectively — after enrolment began, a reporting-bias signal, not disqualifying (25688779) (checked 2026-09-13T08:44:13Z via PubMed efetch (PublicationType + CommentsCorrections) + AACT dates).</p><p>114 records screened; <strong>9 included</strong>. Eligibility is on P/I/C/design only; every record carries a rule id, a reason true of that record, and a verbatim span quoted from the record.</p><table class='recs'><tr><th>Record</th><th>Type</th><th>Decision</th><th>Rule</th><th>Found by</th><th>Reason (true of the record)</th><th>Verbatim span (from the record)</th></tr><tr><td>42425738</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X1</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>not a randomized controlled trial (record: 42425738).</td><td class='span'>publication types: Journal Article, Meta-Analysis, Systematic Review</td></tr><tr><td>40597594</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X1</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>not a randomized controlled trial (record: 40597594).</td><td class='span'>