 is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.&quot; AFTER &quot;TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL — DISCOVERY-BIASED, NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process.&quot;
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>overrides.json (rendered capture)</title><style>body{font:15px/1.5 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:64rem;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;color:#12232e}code{background:#f1f3f5;padding:0 .2em;word-break:break-all}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4em .5em;vertical-align:top;text-align:left}.note{border-left:4px solid #b45309;padding:.5em 1em;background:#fffbeb}.sha{font-size:.85em}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;background:#f8f9fa;padding:1em;border:1px solid #ddd}</style></head><body><h1>overrides.json</h1><p class="note"><strong>This is an HTML rendering of a raw evidence capture.</strong> The text below is the capture verbatim. The raw file is served at <code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/override-audit-2026-09-14/overrides.json</code>; its SHA-256 is <code>d863b104a2629dddf47f072199a865a6cf4e539e4370cdc6656b0be9cb88f795</code> (32,575 bytes). <strong>That digest is of the raw file, not of this HTML page.</strong> The attestation in <code>/_production/manifest.json</code> covers the raw bytes; this page exists only because some fetchers refuse text/plain and text/markdown.</p><p><em>What it proves:</em> Machine-readable rows; tests/test_override_audit.py refuses any override in the tree that is not recorded here with a judgement.</p><pre>[
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:9:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;ELIGIBLE under the registered broad PICO (population is pericarditis \u2014 ACUTE first episode OR recurrent \u2014 treated to prevent recurrence; the protocol was deliberately revised from a recurrent-only draft), so ICAP is NOT refused for population. It is not POOLED because its recurrence-specific outcome is not extractable from an accessible source: the ICAP abstract (NEJM 2013, PMID 23992557) reports only the composite primary \u201cincessant OR recurrent pericarditis\u201d (20/120 vs 45/120), a DIFFERENT endpoint from our \u201crecurrent pericarditis\u201d outcome; the pure-recurrence component (reported as 11/120 vs 25/120 in the full text per an external audit) is full-text-only and the NEJM full text is NOT open-access (no PMC/EPMC, Europe PMC isOpenAccess=N), so we cannot verify it against a committed source span and do not pool an unverifiable number. Were it poolable it would give k=3, RR ~0.474, excluding the null \u2014 consistent with a later randomised-evidence meta (RR 0.48, 0.36\u20130.63) and with our k=2 point estimate. Recorded as not-extracted (full text not retrievable), not a population refusal.&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:23:    &quot;override_replaces&quot;: &quot;Abstract 4-point TECOS composite HR 0.98 (CV death, MI, stroke, or unstable-angina hospitalization).&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:25:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;declared absent (estimand mismatch): TECOS&#x27;s abstract reports its primary as a FOUR-point composite (cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction, nonfatal stroke, OR hospitalization for unstable angina), HR 0.98 (0.88-1.09). Our outcome is 3-point MACE (no unstable-angina hospitalization); TECOS&#x27;s 3-point HR (~0.99) is not in the committed abstract (full text/supplement only). Refuse rather than pool a 4-point estimate under a 3-point label. Surfaced by cross-family (Fable) QA on a page that had passed every internal gate.&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:105:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;declared absent (definition mismatch, cross-family definition audit): the stored 733/6239 vs 745/6266 is Rischio e Prevenzione&#x27;s REVISED primary endpoint &#x27;death from cardiovascular causes or admission to hospital for cardiovascular causes&#x27; (a broad CV-death-or-hospitalization composite), NOT the 3-point major-vascular-events (death/MI/stroke) our outcome names. The abstract states the INITIALLY specified 3-point primary was revised after a lower-than-expected event rate; the 3-point counts are not in the abstract. Refuse rather than pool a broader CV-hospitalization composite under a major-vascular-events label.&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:121:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;declared absent (definition mismatch, cross-family definition audit): OMEGA-REMODEL&#x27;s MACE is an idiosyncratic composite (all-cause death, heart-failure hospitalization, recurrent acute coronary syndrome, late CABG) with NO stroke and NO cardiovascular-death component, in a 6-month post-AMI cardiac-remodeling pilot -- not the death/MI/stroke major-vascular-events endpoint our outcome names. Refuse rather than pool a different composite under a MACE label.&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:137:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;declared absent (population mismatch, cross-family definition audit): the stored RR 0.21 is a PER-PROTOCOL analysis of the 63 patients who &#x27;completed the study according to the protocol&#x27;, not the 87 randomized (46 vs 41). An ITT/randomized-denominator AAD result is not in the abstract. Refuse rather than pool a per-protocol effect where the other trials are ITT.&quot;,
docs\evidence\override-audit-2026-09-14\overrides.json.html:153:    &quot;stated_reason&quot;: &quot;declared absent (population mismatch, cross-family definition audit): the stored 16/106 vs 13/98 are the 204 patients who COMPLETED follow-up, not the 275 randomized (~26% excluded). An ITT/randomized-denominator AAD result is not in the abstract. Refuse rather than pool a completers analysis where the other trials are ITT.&quot;,
docs\evidence\limitation-softening-read-2026-09-14\README.md:1:SOFTENED PAIRS FOUND: 15; first example corticosteroids-cap-mortality b8925e04 pair 1: BEFORE "Search provenance — not a completed systematic search. The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is NOT_RUN ; its evidence set was assembled by KNOWN-ITEM RETRIEVAL of named publications (UID/PMID-anchored queries for pre-identified trials), which cannot discover an unknown eligible trial. A fetch of named identifiers is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic." AFTER "TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL — DISCOVERY-BIASED, NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process."
