2015 (PMID 25688779)\nreports its secondary as 'in-hospital mortality', so no keyword was a substring and\nthe trial was declared-absent -- an all-cause-mortality RCT dropped on a pure\nsynonym gap. Phrase keywords naming death/mortality now also match the swapped\nsynonym ('in-hospital death' <-> 'in-hospital mortality'); bare tokens ('died') are\nNOT broadened, and Torres's primary treatment-failure composite (8/61 vs 18/59, no\ndeath/mortality word) stays correctly unselected.\n\nGeneral across every mortality topic. Corpus effect is surgical: exactly one topic\nmoves. corticosteroids-cap-mortality all-cause mortality k=1 -> k=2 (adds Torres\n6/61 vs 9/59), RR 0.525 (0.33-0.836, significant) -> RR 0.546 (0.036-8.26, NOT\nsignificant): the point estimate barely moves but the honest k=2 HKSJ interval (t1)\nno longer excludes no-effect. The move is toward the null -- the previous k=1\n'significant benefit' was overconfident precisely because it omitted a trial.\n\nDenominator audit (owed): verified already-correct, no change needed -- SELECT\nAE-discontinuation 718/8801 (placebo N right), semaglutide-weight 1306/655 &\n407/204, LoDoCo2 MACE uses source HR (no reconstructed count denominator).\n\nRegression: tests/test_mortality_death_synonym.py (real cached Torres record + spec):\npositive synonym match, binds mortality not treatment-failure, bare token not\nbroadened, both swap directions. Full suite 312 passing; 32/32 reproduce.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:43:42Z","author":{"name":"mahmood726-cyber","email":"mahmood726@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"mahmood726-cyber","email":"mahmood726@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1364922793,"node_id":"R_kgDOUVsRqQ","name":"meta-harness","full_name":"mahmood726-cyber/meta-harness","private":false,"owner":{"login":"mahmood726-cyber","id":227387868,"node_id":"U_kgDODY2p3A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227387868?v=4","gravatar_id":"