codex
One wrinkle surfaced: the benchmark has a single `five audit-named trials` placeholder, while the lane text asks me to look for the five named trials behind it. I’m narrowing that audit trace now so the final JSON can respect the benchmark count and still expose the underlying names as evidence/alternatives where the repo actually contains them.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "python -c \"import json; slugs=['corticosteroids-cap-mortality','dpp4-mace-t2d','empagliflozin-hfpef-hosp','glp1-ra-mace-t2d','iv-iron-hfref-hosp','probiotics-aad-prevention','colchicine-recurrent-pericarditis'];
for s in slugs:
 d=json.load(open(f'docs/reviews/{s}/review.json', encoding='utf-8'))
 print('---',s); print('known_eligible_missing=',d.get('known_eligible_missing')); print('declared_absent=', d.get('primary',{}).get('declared_absent_trials'))\"" in C:\mh-r-R3
exec
