controlled trial: intervention exenatide, comparator placebo, population type 2 diabetes — P/I/C/design met.</td><td class='span'>population “…diovascular Outcomes in Type 2 Diabetes.”; comparator “…ose of 2 mg or matching placebo once weekly. The primar…”</td></tr><tr><td>26630143</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-include'>include</td><td>INCLUDE</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>eligible randomised controlled trial: intervention lixisenatide, comparator placebo, population type 2 diabetes — P/I/C/design met.</td><td class='span'>population “…natide in Patients with Type 2 Diabetes and Acute Coronary Synd…”; comparator “…receive lixisenatide or placebo in addition to locally…”</td></tr><tr><td>37952131</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X2</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>wrong population: title/conditions mention &#x27;without diabetes&#x27;.</td><td class='span'>…lar Outcomes in Obesity without Diabetes.</td></tr><tr><td>34526024</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-exclude'>exclude</td><td>X1</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>not a randomized controlled trial (record: 34526024).</td><td class='span'>publication types: Journal Article, Meta-Analysis, Systematic Review</td></tr><tr><td>SOUL · 40162642</td><td>pmid</td><td class='dec-include'>include</td><td>INCLUDE</td><td>legacy_unrecorded#1</td><td>eligible randomised controlled trial: intervention semaglutide, comparator placebo, population type 2 diabetes — P/I/C/design met.</td><td class='span'>population “…r Outcomes in High-Risk Type 2 Diabetes. SOUL”; comparator “…. In this double-blind, placebo-controlled, event-drive…”</td></tr></table><h4>Controls</h4><ul><li><strong>Positive:</strong> Recovered &amp; included the canonical trials [&#x27;27295427&#x27;, &#x27;27633186&#x27;, &#x27;31189511&#x27;] that a comparator includes; none missed.</li><li><strong>Negative:</strong> Cross-topic trial(s) [&#x27;37952131&#x27;] recovered by the search and correctly EXCLUDED [&#x27;37952131&#x27;] by rule (same drug/design, wrong topic).</li></ul></section><section class="tab" id="tab-outcomes"><h3 class="tabname">Results</h3><h4>3-point major adverse cardiovascular events (primary)</h4><table class='kv'><tr><th>Estimand</th><td>HR</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis population</th><td>intention-to-treat</td></tr><tr><th>Timepoint</th><td>trial end</td></tr><tr><th>Method</th><td>Random-effects inverse-variance on the log ratio (log RR/OR/HR/IRR as configured for the outcome); Paule-Mandel tau^2; HKSJ 95% CI on t_{k-1} (variance floor max(1,Q/(k-1))); prediction interval mu +/- t_{k-1}*sqrt(tau2+se^2). Validated vs metafor 5.0.1 (this canonical code path; every rendered interval is gate-checked to originate here).</td></tr><tr><th>k</th><td>8</td></tr><tr><th>Pooled effect</th><td>0.86 (HR), 95% CI 0.81–0.91</td></tr><tr><th>Prediction interval</th><td>0.81–0.91</td></tr><tr><th>τ²</th><td>4e-05 (non-zero; not 0)</td></tr><tr><th>Leave-one-out (influence)</th><td>estimate ranges 0.84–0.87 across single-trial drops; most influential: 28910237. each row drops one trial and re-pools; a stable estimate across drops = no single trial drives it.</td></tr></table><h5>Compatibility key (pooling contract)</h5><table class='kv'><tr><th>Effect-measure class</th><td>FIRST_EVENT_RATIO</td></tr><tr><th>Effect-measure labels pooled</th><td></td></tr><tr><th>Endpoint</th><td>composite</td></tr><tr><th>Follow-up window</th><td>trial end</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis set</th><td>intention-to-treat</td></tr><tr><th>Randomised contrast (registry-confirmed)</th><td>0 of 8 pooled trials</td></tr></table><p class='note'>k = 8: the 8 trial(s) named below were pooled; 1 further screened-in trial(s) had no poolable value for this outcome and are listed below with an explicit <em>absence state</em>. These are four different things and only one is a claim about the trial: <em>no outcome data in source</em> (the full text was retrieved and is silent — the only state that means the trial itself lacks the outcome; 0 here) vs. <em>not extracted</em> (the number IS in the retrieved source — an extraction gap, about us, not the trial), <em>abstract only, full text not retrieved</em> (absence in the trial is unproven), and <em>excluded on evidence</em> (a number was found and deliberately not pooled — see reason). An unassessed outcome never counts as favourable to the intervention.</p><table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Id</th><th>Input</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>31185157</td><td>PMID 31185157</td><td>0.79 (HR), 95% CI 0.57–1.11 <span class='muted' title='the effect+CI reported by the source'>· source-reported</span></td><td><span class='vok' title='effect present in committed source'>✓ verified against source</span><br>abstract source-reported HR (registered estimand): Major adverse cardiovascular events occurred in 61 of 1591 patients (3.8%) in the oral semaglutide group and 76 of 1592 (4.8%) in the placebo group (hazard ratio, 0.79; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0<div class='ident'><em>design key:</em> UNKNOWN / unit UNKNOWN; estimator PUBLISHED_UNADJUSTED; correlation handling none; action ALLOW_WITH_LABEL</div></td></tr><tr><td>27633186</td><td>PMID 27633186</td><td>0.74 (HR), 95% CI 0.58–0.95 <span class='muted' title='the effect+CI reported by the source'>· source-reported</span></td><td><span class='vok' title='effect present in committed source'>✓ verified against source</span><br>abstract source-reported HR (registered estimand): The primary outcome occurred in 108 of 1648 patients (6.6%) in the semaglutide group and in 146 of 1649 patients (8.9%) in the placebo group (hazard ratio, 0.74; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.58 to <div class='ident'><em>design key:</em> UNKNOWN / unit UNKNOWN; estimator PUBLISHED_UNADJUSTED; correlation handling none; action ALLOW_WITH_LABEL</div></td></tr><tr><td>27295427</td><td>PMID 27295427</td><td>0.87 (HR), 95% CI 0.78–0.97 <span class='muted' title='the effect+CI reported by the source'>· source-reported</spa