docs\reviews\colchicine-recurrent-pericarditis\index.html:85:</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-search"><h3 class="tabname">Search</h3><table class='kv'><tr><th>Records retrieved</th><td>53</td></tr><tr><th>Databases / sources</th><td>PubMed, ClinicalTrials.gov</td></tr><tr><th>Committed cache</th><td>cache/colchicine-recurrent-pericarditis/records.json</td></tr><tr><th>Run (UTC)</th><td>2026-09-11</td></tr></table><h4>Retrieval snapshot</h4><div class='banner'><p><strong>Snapshot:</strong> records_sha256 <code>570a1143</code>; retrieved_utc 2026-09-11; mode LEGACY_UNRECORDED: a pre-ledger fetch; which query retrieved which record was not recorded; every record's found_by names this single source.</p><p>This page is a REPLAY of that snapshot: re-running from the protocol SHA regenerates it byte-for-byte. A live re-search is a separate, dated event (see Re-search below if present).</p></div><h4>Retrieval sources</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Query</th><th>Run date</th><th>State</th><th>hits -&gt; fetched -&gt; retained</th><th>Cap</th><th>Discovery-capable</th></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>colchicine AND pericarditis AND (recurrent OR recurrence) AND (randomized OR randomised OR trial)</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>colchicine pericarditis randomized double-blind placebo</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>LEGACY_UNRECORDED</td><td><code>colchicine AND pericarditis AND (recurrent OR recurrence) AND (randomized OR randomised OR trial) || colchicine pericarditis randomized double-blind placebo</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_OK</strong>: ran and returned records</td><td>unknown -&gt; 50 -&gt; 50</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>no</td></tr></table><h4>Source status (which adapters ran)</h4><p class='muted'>Citation chase: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · ClinicalTrials.gov: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Europe PMC (OA + metadata): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Legacy unrecorded retrieval: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · PMC full text: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · PubMed: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Registry-first (AACT): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> — RAN_OK = ran and returned records; RAN_ZERO = ran, none matched; RAN_ERROR = attempted but failed; NOT_RUN = not attempted for this topic.</p><h4>Retrieval class</h4><div class='absent'><p><strong>HAND-WRITTEN KEYWORD SEARCH — NOT A REGISTERED CONCEPT SEARCH; NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH</strong> We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic. an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process.</p></div><table class='recs'><tr><th>Verbatim query</th><th>Kind</th><th>Features fired</th></tr><tr><td><code>colchicine AND pericarditis AND (recurrent OR recurrence) AND (randomized OR randomised OR trial)</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>colchicine pericarditis randomized double-blind placebo</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>colchicine AND pericarditis AND (recurrent OR recurrence) AND (randomized OR randomised OR trial) || colchicine pericarditis randomized double-blind placebo</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>RAN_OK</strong>; its PubMed queries are hand-written keyword strings that were never registered as a concept search, whose discovery reach is unmeasured — a zero here reads as not observed, never as absent. A hand-written keyword query is not a documented systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>Positive-control recovery (NOT systematic-review recall)</h4><p>Positive-control recovery: the committed registry query re-found <strong>3/3</strong> of this topic's PRE-SPECIFIED known trials (pooled + declared positive controls; enumerated 7; status RAN_OK). <span class='muted'>Measured 2026-09-11T23:39:14Z.</span> <strong>This is not systematic-review recall.</strong> It measures whether the committed registry query re-finds the trials ALREADY KNOWN to the build; a trial that was never in the known set is not in the denominator, so a high value does <strong>not</strong> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>7</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 5 have a linked publication; <strong>0</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 1 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>colchicine AND pericarditis AND (recurrent OR recurrence) AND (randomized OR randomised OR trial)</pre><pre class='query'>colchicine pericarditis randomized double-blind placebo</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;pericarditis&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;colchicine&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier names colchicine; all included records map to that agent. Verdict: <code>MATCH</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n</th></tr><tr><td>Records identified (committed search)</td><td>53</td></tr><tr><td>Records screened (deduplicated)</td><td>53</td></tr><tr><td>Excluded at screening — by rule</td><td>50 (X-DEDUP 3 · X1 30 · X2 9 · X3 8)</td></tr><tr><td>Met eligibility (P/I/C/design)</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pooled in the primary outcome (k)</strong></td><td><strong>2</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Eligible but outcome not extracted from the abstract (full-text pass pending)</td><td>1</td></tr></table><p class='note'>Every excluded record's rule id, reason and verbatim span are listed below (PRISMA item 16b: exclusions with reasons).</p><h4>Dual independent screening (PRISMA item 8)</h4><p>Two independently-implemented rule screeners over 53 records: agreement <strong>49/53</strong>, disagreement <strong>7.5%</strong> (4 records). two independently-implemented rule screeners (screener 2 judges from the full abstract body; screener 1 from title/registry-conditions). Adjudicator: screener 1. <em>the two rule sets share an author and the same eligibility criteria, so they are NOT statistically independent; this agreement overstates inter-rater reliability. A genuinely independent model screener on the embedding shortlist 