 &#x27;cardiopulmonary bypass&#x27;, &#x27;open heart&#x27;, &#x27;open-heart&#x27;, &#x27;heart surgery&#x27;, &#x27;valve surgery&#x27;, &#x27;valvular surgery&#x27;].</td><td class='span'>examined title/conditions/abstract: “Colchicine to Prevent Post-Pericardiotomy Syndrome and Atrial Fibrillation Atrial Fibrilla…”</td></tr></table><h4>Controls</h4><ul><li><strong>Positive:</strong> Recovered &amp; included the canonical trials [&#x27;25172965&#x27;, &#x27;32720823&#x27;] that a comparator includes; none missed.</li><li><strong>Negative:</strong> Cross-topic trial(s) [&#x27;21873705&#x27;] recovered by the search and correctly EXCLUDED [&#x27;21873705&#x27;] by rule (same drug/design, wrong topic).</li></ul></section><section class="tab" id="tab-outcomes"><h3 class="tabname">Results</h3><div class='absent'><strong>Cross-family definition audit.</strong> Two independent model families (Gemini via AGY, and Fable) re-read every pooled row and checked whether the extracted result matches the outcome LABEL's definition &mdash; composite component set, timepoint, population, analysis set &mdash; not just the number. Rows flagged for this topic, with how each was resolved (refuse the trial / disclose the heterogeneity / relabel the timepoint / already disclosed). This is the endpoint-<strong>IDENTITY</strong> check &mdash; distinct from the per-number <strong>MAGNITUDE</strong> check (every pooled number located in its committed source span, gate-enforced). A number can pass magnitude and fail identity, which is exactly the class this audit catches; &lsquo;verified&rsquo; on this harness now means both:<table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Finding</th><th>Resolution</th></tr><tr><td>27502857</td><td>Gastrointestinal adverse effects</td><td>flagged; per-row adjudication</td><td><strong>DISCLOSED (diarrhoea-only counts used as the GI-adverse-effect proxy; open-label trial, no placebo)</strong></td></tr><tr><td>37640035</td><td>Gastrointestinal adverse effects</td><td>flagged; per-row adjudication</td><td><strong>DISCLOSED (prespecified non-infectious-diarrhoea safety outcome reported as events; narrower than a broad GI-adverse-effect endpoint)</strong></td></tr><tr><td>29237033</td><td>Postoperative atrial fibrillation</td><td>Pilot: POAF within 30 days, lung-resection surgery. ·both families</td><td><strong>EXCLUDED as non-cardiac population: Bessissow (lung resection) is outside the protocol I2 cardiac-surgery population. The mismatch was a POPULATION mismatch, not a timepoint one — the earlier timepoint-relabel resolution fixed the wrong axis (external audit). No longer pooled.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>37640035</td><td>Postoperative atrial fibrillation</td><td>COP-AF: 14-day window, clinically-important AF, non-cardiac thoracic surgery. ·both families</td><td><strong>EXCLUDED as non-cardiac population: COP-AF (non-cardiac surgery) is outside the protocol I2 cardiac-surgery population. The mismatch was a POPULATION mismatch, not a timepoint one — the earlier timepoint-relabel resolution fixed the wrong axis (external audit). No longer pooled.</strong></td></tr></table></div><h4>Postoperative atrial fibrillation (primary)</h4><table class='kv'><tr><th>Estimand</th><td>RR</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis population</th><td>intention-to-treat</td></tr><tr><th>Timepoint</th><td>postoperative, in-hospital to 30 days (windows vary by trial: index-admission, 14-day, and 30-day POAF)</td></tr><tr><th>Method</th><td>Random-effects inverse-variance on the log ratio (log RR/OR/HR/IRR as configured for the outcome); Paule-Mandel tau^2; HKSJ 95% CI on t_{k-1} (variance floor max(1,Q/(k-1))); prediction interval mu +/- t_{k-1}*sqrt(tau2+se^2). Validated vs metafor 5.0.1 (this canonical code path; every rendered interval is gate-checked to originate here).</td></tr><tr><th>k</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Pooled effect</th><td>0.67 (RR), 95% CI 0.38–1.21</td></tr><tr><th>Prediction interval</th><td>0.24–1.91</td></tr><tr><th>τ²</th><td>0.0741</td></tr><tr><th>Leave-one-out (influence)</th><td>estimate ranges 0.61–0.79 across single-trial drops; most influential: 42132185. each row drops one trial and re-pools; a stable estimate across drops = no single trial drives it.</td></tr></table><h5>Compatibility key (pooling contract)</h5><table class='kv'><tr><th>Effect-measure class</th><td>FIRST_EVENT_RATIO</td></tr><tr><th>Effect-measure labels pooled</th><td></td></tr><tr><th>Endpoint</th><td>single endpoint</td></tr><tr><th>Follow-up window</th><td>postoperative, in-hospital to 30 days (windows vary by trial: index-admission, 14-day, and 30-day POAF)</td></tr><tr><th>Analysis set</th><td>intention-to-treat</td></tr><tr><th>Randomised contrast (registry-confirmed)</th><td>2 of 4 pooled trials</td></tr></table><p class='note'>k = 4: the 4 trial(s) named below were pooled; 4 further screened-in trial(s) had no poolable value for this outcome and are listed below with an explicit <em>absence state</em>. These are four different things and only one is a claim about the trial: <em>no outcome data in source</em> (the full text was retrieved and is silent — the only state that means the trial itself lacks the outcome; 0 here) vs. <em>not extracted</em> (the number IS in the retrieved source — an extraction gap, about us, not the trial), <em>abstract only, full text not retrieved</em> (absence in the trial is unproven), and <em>excluded on evidence</em> (a number was found and deliberately not pooled — see reason). An unassessed outcome never counts as favourable to the intervention.</p><table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Id</th><th>Input</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>42132185</td><td>PMID 42132185</td><td>0.37 (RR), 95% CI 0.21–0.66 <span class='muted' title='the effect+CI reported by the source'>· source-reported</span></td><td><span class='vok' title='effect present in committed source'>✓ verified against source</span><br>abstract effect+CI (RR): RESULTS: Of 163 analyzed patients (81 colchicine, 