codex
Two fixes are straightforward: one EMPA-VISION design-paper DOI was mistyped from the raw CT.gov citation, and the IRON-HF design-paper alternative needs its own PubMed evidence file listed. For the DOI-only records, I’ll add DOI-resolver JSON captures so the normal, unescaped DOI string is present verbatim.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath .\\lane_r3\\raw | Where-Object { [int]("'$_.Name.Substring(0,3)) -ge 069 -and [int]($_.Name.Substring(0,3)) -le 080 } | Select-Object Name,Length | Format-Table -AutoSize' in C:\mh-r-R3
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "@'
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from pathlib import Path
for n in [52,54,70,72,74,76]:
    files=list(Path('lane_r3/raw').glob(f'{n:03d}-*.xml'))
    if not files: continue
    p=files[0]
    print('\\n##',p.name)
    root=ET.parse(p).getroot()
    for art in root.findall('.//PubmedArticle')[:3]:
        ids=[(a.attrib.get('IdType'), a.text) for a in art.findall('./PubmedData/ArticleIdList/ArticleId')]
        title=art.findtext('./MedlineCitation/Article/ArticleTitle') or ''
        print(art.findtext('./MedlineCitation/PMID'), ids, title.encode('ascii','backslashreplace').decode('ascii'))
'@ | python -" in C:\mh-r-R3
